  "fields": {
    "title": "Web-to-Print",
    "textContent": {
      "nodeType": "document",
      "data": {},
      "content": [
        {
          "nodeType": "heading-3",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "Description",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "paragraph",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "Web-to-Print, also referred to as Web2Print, W2P or Remote Publishing, combines the traditional way of producing print materials, as well as all other processes that take place online, like the creation and publishing process for example. Many different processes, systems and software can be used for Web-To-Print, like the editing of simple templates or creating print materials out of websites or with the help of code.",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink",
              "data": {
                "target": {
                  "sys": {
                    "id": "4YfTaPJ99bPbYx7sboP7Yd",
                    "type": "Link",
                    "linkType": "Entry"
                  }
                }
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "nodeType": "text",
                  "value": "[1]",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "superscript"
                    }
                  ],
                  "data": {}
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "heading-3",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "Examples",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "paragraph",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "Paged.js as an example is a free and open source JavaScript library that paginates content in the browser to create PDF output from any HTML content. This means you can design works for print (e.g. books) using HTML and CSS. Another example is",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": " bindery.js",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "italic"
                }
              ],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": " is a javascript library to create printable books with HTML and CSS. If you want to know, which other web-to-print software exists, take a look at ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "hyperlink",
              "data": {
                "uri": "https://prepostprint.org/"
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "nodeType": "text",
                  "value": "PrePostPrint",
                  "marks": [],
                  "data": {}
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": ".",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
